<title>USA: Searle, Unimed enter marketing pact.</title>
<headline>Searle, Unimed enter marketing pact.</headline>
<dateline>BUFFALO GROVE, Ill. 1997-02-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Searle, the pharmaceutical division of Monsanto Co, said Tuesday it signed a marketing and distribution agreement with Unimed Pharmaceuticals Inc worth an undisclosed amount.</p>
<p>Searle said the deal allows Unimed to market and distribute its fluoroquinolone anti-infective drug Maxaquin in the United States. Unimed will pay sales-based distribution fees as part of the agreement, which goes into effect March 1.</p>
<p>Maxaquin is used to treat bacterial infections following transurethral surgery or transrectal prostate biopsy.</p>
<p>Searle develops pharmaceutical products.</p>
<p>Unimed markets niche pharmaceutical products.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
